{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Credit Card Transaction Anomaly Detection using Isolation Forest\n",
        "\n",
        "**Project Type:** Unsupervised Machine Learning  \n",
        "**Algorithm:** Isolation Forest  \n",
        "**Business Use Case:** Detect unusual / potentially fraudulent credit-card transactions.\n",
        "\n",
        "This notebook covers data loading, EDA, feature engineering, Isolation Forest training, anomaly scoring, evaluation, visualization, model persistence, and prediction on a new transaction.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Install packages if needed:\n",
        "# !pip install pandas numpy matplotlib seaborn scikit-learn joblib\n",
        "\n",
        "import warnings\n",
        "warnings.filterwarnings(\"ignore\")\n",
        "\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "import seaborn as sns\n",
        "import joblib\n",
        "\n",
        "from sklearn.ensemble import IsolationForest\n",
        "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n",
        "from sklearn.metrics import classification_report, confusion_matrix, roc_auc_score\n",
        "\n",
        "pd.set_option(\"display.max_columns\", None)\n",
        "sns.set_theme(style=\"whitegrid\")\n",
        "RANDOM_STATE = 42\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 1. Load Dataset"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "df = pd.read_csv(\"credit_card_transactions.csv\", parse_dates=[\"transaction_datetime\"])\n",
        "print(\"Dataset shape:\", df.shape)\n",
        "display(df.head())\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 2. Data Quality Checks"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "print(\"Data types:\")\n",
        "display(df.dtypes.to_frame(\"dtype\"))\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Missing values:\")\n",
        "display(df.isnull().sum().to_frame(\"missing\"))\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Duplicate rows:\", df.duplicated().sum())\n",
        "\n",
        "display(df.describe().T)\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 3. Exploratory Data Analysis"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "plt.figure(figsize=(9,5))\n",
        "sns.histplot(df[\"transaction_amount\"], bins=60, kde=True)\n",
        "plt.title(\"Transaction Amount Distribution\")\n",
        "plt.xlabel(\"Transaction Amount\")\n",
        "plt.show()\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "plt.figure(figsize=(9,5))\n",
        "sns.boxplot(x=df[\"transaction_amount\"])\n",
        "plt.title(\"Transaction Amount Box Plot\")\n",
        "plt.show()\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "plt.figure(figsize=(9,5))\n",
        "sns.countplot(data=df, x=\"transaction_hour\")\n",
        "plt.title(\"Transactions by Hour\")\n",
        "plt.xlabel(\"Hour\")\n",
        "plt.ylabel(\"Count\")\n",
        "plt.show()\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "plt.figure(figsize=(10,7))\n",
        "sns.heatmap(df.select_dtypes(\"number\").corr(), annot=True, fmt=\".2f\",\n",
        "            cmap=\"coolwarm\", center=0)\n",
        "plt.title(\"Correlation Heatmap\")\n",
        "plt.show()\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 4. Feature Engineering"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "df[\"amount_log\"] = np.log1p(df[\"transaction_amount\"])\n",
        "df[\"is_night\"] = ((df[\"transaction_hour\"] < 6) | (df[\"transaction_hour\"] >= 23)).astype(int)\n",
        "df[\"high_velocity\"] = (df[\"transactions_last_24h\"] >= 8).astype(int)\n",
        "df[\"high_distance\"] = (df[\"distance_from_home_km\"] >= 50).astype(int)\n",
        "\n",
        "features = [\n",
        "    \"amount_log\", \"transaction_hour\", \"distance_from_home_km\",\n",
        "    \"merchant_risk_score\", \"transactions_last_24h\", \"device_change_count\",\n",
        "    \"account_age_days\", \"failed_attempts\", \"international_transaction\",\n",
        "    \"is_night\", \"high_velocity\", \"high_distance\"\n",
        "]\n",
        "\n",
        "X = df[features]\n",
        "print(\"Feature matrix shape:\", X.shape)\n",
        "print(\"Features:\", features)\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 5. Feature Scaling"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "scaler = StandardScaler()\n",
        "X_scaled = scaler.fit_transform(X)\n",
        "print(\"Scaling completed.\")\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 6. Train Isolation Forest"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "model = IsolationForest(\n",
        "    n_estimators=300,\n",
        "    contamination=0.05,\n",
        "    max_samples=\"auto\",\n",
        "    max_features=1.0,\n",
        "    random_state=RANDOM_STATE,\n",
        "    n_jobs=-1\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "model.fit(X_scaled)\n",
        "\n",
        "df[\"model_prediction\"] = model.predict(X_scaled)\n",
        "df[\"predicted_anomaly\"] = (df[\"model_prediction\"] == -1).astype(int)\n",
        "df[\"anomaly_score\"] = -model.decision_function(X_scaled)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Predicted classes:\")\n",
        "print(df[\"predicted_anomaly\"].value_counts())\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 7. Detected Anomalies"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "anomalies = df[df[\"predicted_anomaly\"] == 1].copy()\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Total transactions:\", len(df))\n",
        "print(\"Detected anomalies:\", len(anomalies))\n",
        "print(\"Anomaly rate:\", round(len(anomalies) / len(df) * 100, 2), \"%\")\n",
        "\n",
        "display(anomalies.sort_values(\"anomaly_score\", ascending=False)[[\n",
        "    \"transaction_id\", \"transaction_datetime\", \"transaction_amount\",\n",
        "    \"distance_from_home_km\", \"merchant_risk_score\",\n",
        "    \"transactions_last_24h\", \"failed_attempts\",\n",
        "    \"international_transaction\", \"anomaly_score\"\n",
        "]].head(20))\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 8. Anomaly Visualization"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "plt.figure(figsize=(10,6))\n",
        "sns.scatterplot(\n",
        "    data=df,\n",
        "    x=\"distance_from_home_km\",\n",
        "    y=\"transaction_amount\",\n",
        "    hue=\"predicted_anomaly\",\n",
        "    alpha=.65\n",
        ")\n",
        "plt.yscale(\"log\")\n",
        "plt.title(\"Isolation Forest \u2014 Detected Anomalies\")\n",
        "plt.xlabel(\"Distance From Home (km)\")\n",
        "plt.ylabel(\"Transaction Amount (log scale)\")\n",
        "plt.show()\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "plt.figure(figsize=(10,5))\n",
        "sns.histplot(\n",
        "    data=df, x=\"anomaly_score\", hue=\"predicted_anomaly\",\n",
        "    bins=50, element=\"step\", stat=\"density\", common_norm=False\n",
        ")\n",
        "plt.title(\"Anomaly Score Distribution\")\n",
        "plt.xlabel(\"Anomaly Score\")\n",
        "plt.show()\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 9. Optional Model Evaluation"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# actual_anomaly is available because this is a synthetic dataset.\n",
        "# For a real unsupervised dataset, true labels may not exist.\n",
        "\n",
        "y_true = df[\"actual_anomaly\"]\n",
        "y_pred = df[\"predicted_anomaly\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Confusion Matrix:\")\n",
        "print(confusion_matrix(y_true, y_pred))\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nClassification Report:\")\n",
        "print(classification_report(y_true, y_pred, digits=4))\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"ROC-AUC:\", round(roc_auc_score(y_true, df[\"anomaly_score\"]), 4))\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 10. Highest-Risk Transactions"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "risk = df.sort_values(\"anomaly_score\", ascending=False).head(25)\n",
        "\n",
        "display(risk[[\n",
        "    \"transaction_id\", \"transaction_datetime\", \"transaction_amount\",\n",
        "    \"distance_from_home_km\", \"merchant_risk_score\",\n",
        "    \"transactions_last_24h\", \"device_change_count\",\n",
        "    \"failed_attempts\", \"international_transaction\",\n",
        "    \"anomaly_score\", \"predicted_anomaly\"\n",
        "]])\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 11. Save Results and Model"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "df.to_csv(\"isolation_forest_transaction_results.csv\", index=False)\n",
        "joblib.dump(model, \"isolation_forest_model.joblib\")\n",
        "joblib.dump(scaler, \"transaction_feature_scaler.joblib\")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Saved:\")\n",
        "print(\"- isolation_forest_transaction_results.csv\")\n",
        "print(\"- isolation_forest_model.joblib\")\n",
        "print(\"- transaction_feature_scaler.joblib\")\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 12. Test a New Transaction"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "new_transaction = pd.DataFrame([{\n",
        "    \"transaction_amount\": 8500,\n",
        "    \"transaction_hour\": 2,\n",
        "    \"distance_from_home_km\": 180,\n",
        "    \"merchant_risk_score\": 0.92,\n",
        "    \"transactions_last_24h\": 15,\n",
        "    \"device_change_count\": 4,\n",
        "    \"account_age_days\": 60,\n",
        "    \"failed_attempts\": 4,\n",
        "    \"international_transaction\": 1\n",
        "}])\n",
        "\n",
        "new_transaction[\"amount_log\"] = np.log1p(new_transaction[\"transaction_amount\"])\n",
        "new_transaction[\"is_night\"] = (\n",
        "    (new_transaction[\"transaction_hour\"] < 6) |\n",
        "    (new_transaction[\"transaction_hour\"] >= 23)\n",
        ").astype(int)\n",
        "new_transaction[\"high_velocity\"] = (new_transaction[\"transactions_last_24h\"] >= 8).astype(int)\n",
        "new_transaction[\"high_distance\"] = (new_transaction[\"distance_from_home_km\"] >= 50).astype(int)\n",
        "\n",
        "new_scaled = scaler.transform(new_transaction[features])\n",
        "prediction = model.predict(new_scaled)[0]\n",
        "score = -model.decision_function(new_scaled)[0]\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Prediction:\", \"ANOMALY / HIGH RISK\" if prediction == -1 else \"NORMAL\")\n",
        "print(\"Anomaly score:\", round(float(score), 4))\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 13. Business Recommendations\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Send high-risk transactions to a fraud-review queue.\n",
        "2. Apply additional authentication to very high-risk transactions.\n",
        "3. Investigate unusual amount, distance, device, velocity, and failed-attempt patterns.\n",
        "4. Tune `contamination` using historical validation data.\n",
        "5. Retrain periodically as fraud behavior changes.\n",
        "6. Monitor false positives and model drift.\n",
        "7. In production, combine Isolation Forest with business rules and supervised fraud models when labels are available.\n",
        "\n",
        "## 14. Project Summary\n",
        "\n",
        "**Input:** Transaction behavior features  \n",
        "**Model:** Isolation Forest  \n",
        "**Output:** Normal / Anomaly and anomaly score\n",
        "\n",
        
      ]
    }
  ],
